    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Atlassian is a public company founded in 2002 and headquartered in Sydney, Australia. On its website, the company describes itself as providing collaboration software for software, IT, and business teams, with products including Jira, Confluence, Trello, Loom, and Rovo AI agents. It presents these as one connected platform for planning, tracking, and delivering work.\n\nAtlassian's AI-related products include Confluence AI and Trello AI. Confluence AI is described as a team wiki AI with smart links, automation, and Atlassian Cloud governance. Trello AI is described as a project management AI with workflow automation and team data exposure under Atlassian Cloud governance. The company's site also mentions Rovo AI agents.\n\nAtlassian trades under the ticker TEAM and has SEC Central Index Key 0001650372. In its most recent 10-K, for the fiscal year ended June 30, 2025, the company reported revenue of $5,215,304,000.",
